 A first-person Pac-Man clone for Roblox, built with Rojo, strict Luau, and Lune for headless tests. New machine: see `SETUP.md`. The game is the `pickman` project, in `pickman/` (its `src/`, specs, Rojo projects and issues, `pickman/.tracker/`); the tooling that tracks and gates it is `z-nile/` (zz-rules skill, Projects). The arcade's projects are registered too (c0183): `arcade/` (the library every place shares), `portal/` (the experience's start place) and the games `snake/`, `invaders/` and `asteroids/`; each keeps its product decisions in `<name>/.tracker/game-design.md`, and the library its design in `arcade/.tracker/architecture.md`. Every project with code has the same home as `pickman/` (c0184): `check.sh`, `.luaurc`, `default.project.json`, `src/`, `tests/` and `skills/`, which the gate checks for each registered project (z-nile/README.md, A project's home).
 
-**Non-negotiable:** no code without a tracker issue, and work is done only when its `check.sh` passes. **Every change is made in a git worktree under `.worktree/` and lands by pull request** (a capture lands with `./zn land`, after a local full gate); the main checkout is never edited, except by `./zn` itself (`ready`, `stop`, `sync`, and the board refresh after every publish or `land`), which only fast-forwards it, clears ignored files from item folders that left it, and writes ignored files (`prompt.md`, `.cache/board.html`, the dispatcher's run state in `.cache/dispatch/`) (zz-rules skill, Worktrees and Landing a change). Start execution with `/z-run <R-id>` in a session in the main checkout: that is z-work with that raft named (`./zn work <R-id>`). With no raft named, run `./zn work`. The unattended launcher stays `./zn dispatch <id>` (zz-rules skill, Dispatch; `.models.toml` names the models). Before doing anything, read the skill that applies. The skills hold all the rules.
+**Non-negotiable:** no code without a tracker issue, and work is done only when its `check.sh` passes. **Every change is made in a git worktree under `.worktree/` and lands by pull request** (a capture lands with `./zn land`, after a local full gate); the main checkout is never edited, except by `./zn` itself (`ready`, `stop`, `sync`, and the board refresh after every publish or `land`), which only fast-forwards it, clears ignored files from item folders that left it, and writes ignored files (`prompt.md`, `.cache/board.html`, the dispatcher's run state in `.cache/dispatch/`) (zz-rules skill, Worktrees and Landing a change). Start execution with `/z-run <R-id>` in a session in the main checkout: that is z-work with that raft named (`./zn work <R-id>`). With no raft named, run z-work: it starts the supervisor, `./zn work --detach --cli <your CLI>` (`./zn work status`, `./zn work stop`), a program that runs no model and sends each pick through the dispatcher. The unattended launcher stays `./zn dispatch <id>` (zz-rules skill, Dispatch; `.models.toml` names the models). Before doing anything, read the skill that applies. The skills hold all the rules.
 
 **Subagents:** don't use `fork` subagents. Delegate to a plain subagent (general-purpose) with `model: "sonnet"` and a full brief. The exceptions are design and code reviewers, which the skills pin to Opus 5.5.
 
-**Processes:** Run every probe, experiment, loop and background command you start yourself (anything that is not the gate, a check, a `./zn` command or the spec runner) through `./zn run --time <seconds> -- <command>`: it stops at its limit, when it ends and when you do. A PreToolUse hook refuses a bare `lune run` of a probe, a loop that never ends and a background job nothing bounds, and `./zn reap` stops what still leaks. A `/clear` ends the background commands of the conversation it clears (the SessionEnd hook stops its tool shells). A subagent stays open while its background commands run, and a command it started stops at its own `./zn run` limit (at most an hour) or at the session's end; the session-end reaper catches anything left. The zz-test skill's "Bounded commands" has the rest.
+**Processes:** Run every probe, experiment, loop and background command you start yourself (anything that is not the gate, a check, a `./zn` command or the spec runner) through `./zn run --time <seconds> -- <command>`: it stops at its limit, when it ends and when you do. A PreToolUse hook refuses a bare `lune run` of a probe, a loop that never ends and a background job nothing bounds, and `./zn reap` stops what still leaks (except the one detached worker supervisor that `./zn work --detach` starts and `.cache/work/state` names: `./zn work stop` ends it). A `/clear` ends the background commands of the conversation it clears (the SessionEnd hook stops its tool shells). A subagent stays open while its background commands run, and a command it started stops at its own `./zn run` limit (at most an hour) or at the session's end; the session-end reaper catches anything left. The zz-test skill's "Bounded commands" has the rest.
 
 **No check may ever change the real repository.** Specs, `check.sh` files and the scripts they run change only throwaway fixtures under `.cache/`. The runner enforces it. On macOS it runs specs in a jail that denies every write to the repository outside `.cache`; a run that can't be jailed (inside another sandbox) refuses to start unless that sandbox already protects the repository. Everywhere it fences git into `.cache`, refuses ref updates and pushes into the real repository, runs one suite per checkout and project home at a time, and fails any run during which the remotes, config, branch or history changed. What it can't see (unjailed runs on Linux, `check.sh` files' own commands, work handed to processes outside the jail), review must catch (zz-test skill, "Specs never touch the real repository"). If its tripwire fires, stop and report: never repair the shared git configuration yourself.
 
