+A raft is delivered as a **stacked PR set**, one layer (a branch and a PR) per issue, in the raft's Order. One worker builds the layers one at a time, each complete (finished, green and reviewed) before the next starts. Each layer is reviewed and gated on its own diff. The stack lands as one `--no-ff` bind of its top layer, with one full gate on its top; a blocked layer stops the layers above it, and the green layers below it land now as a shorter bind (`./zn done <R-id> --through <issue>`). Each landing has its own final review and trace, and the layers above an early landing are restacked onto `main`. A one-issue raft is a stack of one. *exists* (c0248)
